{
 "text": "Governments all over Europe just shut down a bunch of their own websites on purpose because of this bug where hackers could take over a site without a password. It's in PHP, the language everyone loves and about 7 out of 10 websites run on it. This bug was in there for like 14 years before researchers using AI figured out how bad it was. They gave the PHP people a heads up, but word got out before the fix was ready and hackers were already trying to use it. Cloudflare says that once it was announced, they saw tens of thousands of hacking attempts in 45 minutes and millions within a day. But even with the fix out, somebody still has to install it on every single server. Plus, something like half of PHP sites run versions so old they're not officially supported anymore. Even the FBI said, if you can't update yet, just turn it off. Which is basically Tech Support's answer to everything. And some of those governments did it before there was even a fix.",
